  "method": [
    "Scratch allocation is retried at smaller capacities before executing any prefill layer. Absolute RoPE positions, causal/sliding-window limits and preceding KV are retained; existing GPU kernel source and the reference agreement policy are unchanged.",
    "The exact extracted CI archive, executable, GGUF and harness digests are retained. All model/GPU work runs remotely; every owned model/client process is stopped before its parent command returns.",
    "All six required ROCm models retain the 4K/F32/single-slot policy. Reference commit and serial/F32 settings remain pinned, with HIP for Qwen and Vulkan for Gemma explicitly identified per row.",
    "There are 288 exact ordinary CLI choices, 72 tokenizer cases and 54 ordinary full HTTP reference replays. Gemma 31B adds 48 forced-small-chunk choices and nine full reference replays at 8K. Qwen 3.8 MTP-off also matches 48 choices.",
    "The first one-query-per-launch prototype times out. The corrected development binary passes the 8K gate but its 300-second coding trial times out; neither failure is overwritten by later runs.",
    "Actual OpenCode 1.19.4 runs directly against the exact CI executable, with one fresh server per fixture, 8K context, 2048 output tokens, 16 steps and a separately labeled 600-second budget. Frozen independent tests fail before each task; no supervisor edits or tool repairs are used.",
    "The long-history replay retains its failed aggregate because the previous package differs from the reference text. The candidate separately matches the complete reference text and returns both stored codes. Its single cold-request latency is diagnostic, not a headline throughput benchmark.",
    "Subsequent changes allow CPU-only checks on stacked PR bases and add documentation/evidence. Tested Zig/Python source hashes still match the current tree; protected launch workflows and hardware/model policy are unchanged."
